WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:06.520
All right, moving on to another use case of the CTAs.

00:06.840 --> 00:13.320
We can use it in order to create our data marts to make it physical data mart instead of virtual data

00:13.320 --> 00:14.560
marts using views.

00:14.560 --> 00:16.360
So let's understand what this means now.

00:16.360 --> 00:20.600
As we learned before, if you have a data warehouse system, our data warehouse, they are going to

00:20.600 --> 00:22.240
store the data inside tables.

00:22.240 --> 00:28.240
But for the second layer the data marts, we can go and use views in order to have dynamic and flexibility

00:28.240 --> 00:30.760
in order to generate multiple data marts.

00:31.000 --> 00:33.440
And we called it the virtual layer.

00:33.440 --> 00:39.560
But now in some scenarios, if things get complicated, your data mart and reports can be slow because

00:39.560 --> 00:42.520
therefore each action you are generating a query.

00:42.520 --> 00:47.840
So the power BI reports and dashboards are creating queries on your data marts, and your data marts

00:47.840 --> 00:52.920
have always to go to the data warehouse in order to retrieve the data for the reports.

00:52.920 --> 00:56.280
And the whole thing could take minutes or maybe sometimes hours.

00:56.520 --> 01:01.160
So in these scenarios, we cannot stay using views because they are slowing everything down.

01:01.160 --> 01:05.720
But instead of that, we have to convert our data mart to a physical layer.

01:05.760 --> 01:11.540
That means instead of using views, we have to go and use tables and one very common way in order to

01:11.540 --> 01:17.940
generate the tables of the data marts on daily basis is to use CTAs queries between the data warehouse

01:17.940 --> 01:19.500
layer and the data mart layer.

01:19.500 --> 01:21.260
It's still going to take maybe 30 minutes.

01:21.260 --> 01:23.820
That's why you can go and prepare the data at the night.

01:23.820 --> 01:28.820
But at the reporting layer where things and the performance really matters, the performance can be

01:28.820 --> 01:33.980
better because the response time from the tables is way faster than views, and the reports don't have

01:33.980 --> 01:38.660
always to waste time waiting for the data marts to get data from the warehouse.

01:38.660 --> 01:44.060
So this is another use case where we use CTAs, where the views at the data marts are slow, and we

01:44.060 --> 01:48.140
have to go and replace them with tables using CTAs to speed up things.

01:48.140 --> 01:51.820
But still, my recommendation here is that start first with the views.

01:51.820 --> 01:56.980
So create a virtual data mart using views, because the implementation is going to be very dynamic and

01:56.980 --> 02:00.260
fast, and you are always getting fresh data from the warehouse.

02:00.260 --> 02:06.340
But maybe later if you notice, okay, some data marts and models are complex, then maybe go and replace

02:06.380 --> 02:09.940
few marts from views to a tables using CTAs.

02:10.100 --> 02:15.220
So this is another use case for the CTAs, and it is a nice workaround for your data warehouse system.
